       These  legacy functions are simpler to use than the X/Open _c_u_r_s_e_s func‐
       tions:

       •   The ggeettaattttrrss function returns the same attribute data as wwaattttrr__ggeett.

           However, ggeettaattttrrss returns an integer  (actually  a  cchhttyyppee),  while
           wwaattttrr__ggeett  returns  the current color pair in a separate parameter.
           In the wide-character library configuration, color  pairs  may  not
           fit into a cchhttyyppee, so wwaattttrr__ggeett is the only way to obtain the color
           information.

           Because ggeettaattttrrss returns the attributes in a single  parameter,  it
           would  not  be possible for an application to distinguish that from
           EERRRR (a _-_1).  If the window  parameter  is  null,  ggeettaattttrrss  returns
           AA__NNOORRMMAALL (zero).

       •   The ggeettbbeeggyy and ggeettbbeeggxx functions return the same data as ggeettbbeeggyyxx.

       •   The ggeettccuurryy and ggeettccuurrxx functions return the same data as ggeettyyxx.

       •   The ggeettmmaaxxyy and ggeettmmaaxxxx functions return the same data as ggeettmmaaxxyyxx.

       •   The ggeettppaarryy and ggeettppaarrxx functions return the same data as ggeettppaarryyxx.

